  data: {
    hero: {
      title: 'FAN TAN (SEVENS)',
      subtitle: 'Card Game',
    },
    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Fan Tan (Sevens)',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Fan Tan, also widely known as 'Sevens', 'Domino', or 'Parliament', is a classic layout-based card game where the objective is to be the first to get rid of all your cards. Players build upon a central layout of cards, starting with the Sevens and expanding outward to the Ace and Two in each suit. It is a game of both luck and light strategy, as players can choose to hold back key 'blocking' cards to prevent opponents from playing.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Originating in the 19th century or earlier, the game has many names across different cultures: 'Parliament' in the UK, 'Domino' or 'Sevens' in many Western countries, and 'Fan Tan' (distinct from the Chinese gambling game of the same name).",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3 to 8 players. 4 to 6 is considered optimal.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Standard 52-card pack. Cards rank A-K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6-5-4-3-2 (Ace high).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards only.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Dealer shuffles and player to dealer's right may cut. Dealer deals all cards one at a time, clockwise, starting with player to dealer's left. Some players may have one more card than others - this does not matter.",
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
