          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first player to shed all cards from your hand.',
          gameplay: "1. Starting: The player to the dealer's left (or the holder of the 7 of Diamonds in some variants) begins.\n2. Valid Plays: You can only play a card if it is:\n   nd A Seven (starts a new row for a suit).\n   nd One higher or one lower than a card already in the layout (e.g., if the 7 of Hearts is on the table, you can play the 6 or 8 of Hearts).\n3. Sequencing: Suits build up from 7 to Ace and down from 7 to 2.\n4. Passing: If you cannot play a valid card, you MUST pass. In some groups, you must pay a fine (one chip) into a pot.",
          keyRules: [
            'No skipping: You cannot play an 8 unless the 7 of that suit is present.',
            'Must play: If you have a legal move, you cannot pass.',
            'Table Layout: Cards are arranged in four rows, one for each suit.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Keep hold of your Sevens if you have cards at the extreme ends of that suit (Aces or 2s). By not playing the 7, you block everyone else from playing in that suit.',
          intermediate: 'Block and Release: If you have both the 6 and 8 of a suit, you control the expansion. You can hold them to prevent others from playing their 5s and 9s.',
          advanced: 'Watch the Discards: In variants where you pay a chip for passing, force your opponents to pass by withholding the midndrange cards (6s and 8s) for as long as possible.',
          tips: [
            'Prioritize playing cards from suits where you have many cards, as this opens up spaces for your own cards to be played.',
            "If you are close to winning, play your 'blockers' to let the game finish before you get stuck with an endndcard.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
